# generated by make_cpl_config.py -- stage-3 coupled fine-tune
# atm parent E02-FT.aug26.atm.A0_B32_C1_L0_O5_W0_X0.S01   (same atm as E19-CFT)
# ocn parent E13-FT.aug26.ocn.A0_B16_C0_L0_O5_W2_X0.S01   (differs from E19-CFT)
#
# The other half of the ocean-loss-weighting triptych, on the CO2 atmosphere
# rather than the baseline one. Against E19-CFT the config differs in exactly
# one line -- the ocean's parameter_init.weights_path -- so this asks the same
# question E20-CFT asks of E18-CFT (does a differently-weighted ocean seed a
# better coupled model?), but on a second, independent atmosphere. Agreement
# between the E18->E20 and E19->E21 deltas is what would make an ocean-weight
# effect credible; disagreement would say the effect is atm-arm-specific.
#
# --nodes 8 to match this atm parent's own global batch (B32), per campaign
# convention: the coupled run's batch tracks whichever arm is being extended,
# not a fixed default.
#
# E13-FT (W2) verified healthy before use: 4 best_inference_ckpt.tar saves,
# no rollout divergence. Both realms initialize from best_inference_ckpt.tar,
# matching every other stage-3 run this campaign.
FME_NODES=8
FME_RANKS=32
FME_PRIORITY=1
WANDB_NAME=E21-CFT.aug26.cpl.A0_B32_C1_L0_O5_W2_X0.S01
WANDB_RUN_GROUP=aug26.cpl.E21-CFT
